{
  "id": "29400_shizumeru",
  "headword": "{鎮|しず}める",
  "reading": "しずめる",
  "romaji": "shizumeru",
  "part_of_speech": "verb (ichidan)",
  "gloss": "to quell; to calm; to suppress",
  "definitions": [
    {
      "sense_number": 1,
      "gloss": "to quell; to calm; to suppress",
      "explanation": "To bring something turbulent under control — a rebellion, a commotion, pain, or one's anger. The transitive partner of {鎮|しず}まる (to subside, to die down)."
    }
  ],
  "examples": [
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex1",
      "japanese": "⟦{反乱|はんらん}→反乱：11860_hanran⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鎮|しず}める。",
      "english": "to quell a rebellion",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex2",
      "japanese": "⟦{薬|くすり}→薬：00793_kusuri⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鎮|しず}める。",
      "english": "to relieve pain with medicine",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    },
    {
      "id": "29400_shizumeru_ex3",
      "japanese": "⟦{彼|かれ}→彼：01292_kare⟧⟦は→は：00079_ha⟧⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{鎮|しず}めよう⟦と→と：00512_to⟧⟦{深呼吸|しんこきゅう}→深呼吸：13294_shinkokyuu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧⟦した→する：00392_suru⟧。",
      "english": "He took a deep breath to calm his anger.",
      "sense_numbers": [
        1
      ],
      "has_audio": false,
      "notes": null
    }
  ],
  "notes": "TRANSITIVITY: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive). Pattern: X ⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧ {鎮|しず}める (quell X). The intransitive partner is ⟦{鎮|しず}まる→鎮まる：17755_shizumaru⟧ (to subside, to die down).\n\nUSAGE:\nTypical objects are disturbances and strong feelings: ⟦{反乱|はんらん}→反乱：11860_hanran⟧ (rebellion), ⟦{騒|さわ}ぎ→騒ぎ：02827_sawagi⟧ (commotion), ⟦{痛|いた}み→痛み：01795_itami⟧ (pain), ⟦{怒|いか}り→怒り：01780_ikari⟧ (anger).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS (same reading しずめる):\n- ⟦{静|しず}める→静める：19446_shizumeru⟧: to quiet (noise, a crowd) — to make calm or quiet\n- ⟦{沈|しず}める→沈める：02060_shizumeru⟧: to sink (something) — to send under water",
